          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Who does guidance describe as a priority group for influenza vaccination?",
          "answer": "The retrieved guidance does not name priority groups for influenza vaccination. The main influenza document says the opposite. It describes routine annual vaccination for everyone aged 6 months and older who has no contraindication, \"rather than restricting it to high-risk groups\" (*Influenza: annual vaccination and the timing of antiviral treatment*).\n\nTwo other documents recommend annual influenza vaccination for people with specific conditions, but they do not call these groups a priority:\n\n- *COPD: spirometric diagnosis, group assessment and initial therapy* says vaccination against influenza reduces flare-ups (exacerbations) in COPD.\n- *Coronary artery disease: secondary prevention after a diagnosis* lists annual influenza vaccination as a heart-protecting measure after a coronary artery diagnosis.\n\nThe retrieved passages do not say which groups, if any, should be first in line when vaccine supply is limited. For that, you could ask a clinician or check your national immunization schedule.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
